    "updated_at": "2022-10-20T13:20:48Z",
    "body": "Looks like this is fixed in master 49995301ce90a0f63b2d5f9cbb30021a0f08f6ff, so the next starship release should be fine (and existing envs after updating the generated init script).\r\n\r\n[`term size`](https://www.nushell.sh/book/commands/term_size.html) had the parameters `-c` and `-r` to get only the columns or rows respectively. This was removed in https://github.com/nushell/nushell/pull/6651 released with nushell version 0.70.\r\n\r\nWithout the `-c` parameter, columns and rows are returned, but the ` | get columns` filter to only get columns was already in place. As such, removing only `-c` like suggested and implemented in 49995301ce90a0f63b2d5f9cbb30021a0f08f6ff is correct.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
