    "updated_at": "2022-10-22T09:51:31Z",
    "body": "> This only works for Unix systems 😭 Didn't find a bypass for windows though...\r\n\r\nOn Windows you can in the nu shell use `config env` and comment out\r\n\r\n```\r\n#starship init nu | save ~/.cache/starship/init.nu\r\n```\r\n\r\nand then fix the `init.nu` script by removing the `-c` from `term size`.\r\n\r\nNotably, this comments out the automatic generating of `init.nu` by starship on launch. As long as there are no substantial changes, that is not an issue. I for one will (try to) remember to reenable it after installing the next Starship version, which I expect to have the change and fix mentioned in its release notes - which should serve as a reminder for me too.\r\n\r\nI’m sure you could adjust the generating with nu logic too, but for me learning and coding that is not worth it for a short term workaround.",
